      "problem": "${}_{20}{P}_{5}=$",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for ${}_{n}{P}_{r}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}\\,.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=20$ and $r=5$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{20}{P}_{5} & =\\frac{20!}{(20-5)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{20!}{15!} \\\\  & =\\frac{20\\cdot 19\\cdot 18\\cdot 17\\cdot 16\\cdot \\cancel{15!}}{\\cancel{15!}} \\\\  & =20\\cdot 19\\cdot 18\\cdot 17\\cdot 16 \\\\  & =1\\,860\\,480.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
